// Title: PUA - Advanced Port Scanner Execution
// Sigma ID: 54773c5f-f1cc-4703-9126-2f797d96a69d
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-12-18 | Modified: 2023-02-07
// ATT&CK: discovery, T1046, T1135
// Description: Detects the use of Advanced Port Scanner.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administrative use
//   - Tools with similar commandline (very rare)
// References:
//   - https://github.com/3CORESec/MAL-CL/tree/master/Descriptors/Other/Advanced%20Port%20Scanner
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_pua_advanced_port_scanner.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath contains "\\advanced_port_scanner" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName contains "advanced_port_scanner" or ProcessVersionInfoFileDescription contains "Advanced Port Scanner") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "/portable" and ProcessCommandLine contains "/lng")
